       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nYou may have a reason for this dose, so tell me which of these you want:\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the max standard dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll add a note that the dose is above the usual maximum and was intentional. I'll do this if you confirm.\n3. **Enter 10 mg PO twice daily**, if you want the same total daily dose. Once-daily dosing is standard because of amlodipine's long half-life.\n\nIf the goal is better BP control, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic may work better than going past 10 mg."
      }
